# Laravel API Rules

- Design APIs from documented use cases and contracts, not from database tables alone.
- Use explicit versioning strategy (for example `/api/v1`) according to the project API document.
- Validate every external input with Form Requests or equivalent.
- Authorize every protected operation using policies/permissions before business execution.
- Return stable response envelopes and error shapes defined by the API documentation.
- Never accept client-provided final delivery status, commission, payout, refund, or authoritative price without server validation.
- Use idempotency keys for retryable critical commands where defined.
- Use HTTP status codes consistently.
- Paginate list endpoints that can grow.
- Avoid N+1 queries through deliberate loading/aggregation.
- Do not expose internal fields, secrets, provider identifiers, or sensitive personal data unnecessarily.
- Document new endpoints and update corresponding use cases/tests.
